In the one-variable case, extrema can occur either in the interior of theinterval or else at the endpoints. 
THerefore, you must compare the values of f at any interior critical points with those at the endpoints to determine which is largest and smallest. 
In the case of functions of n variables, we do something similar, namely, compare the vales of functions of f at any critical points with values at any restricted critical points that may occur along the boundary of the domain. 
